`AModelProp11.prop11` assumes, as data, integer factorizations `fac A = (E₁, Π, E₂)` with
`A = E₁ Π E₂` **over `ℤ`** (`FacAt`). This cannot be produced in general from Lemma 9 (the
factors are rational, and their reductions mod `q ^ b` are `q`-adic, not integral). This file:

0. `bruhat_lower`: a copy of `Solutions/Bruhat.lean` (Lemma 9 over a field), renamed.
1. `ratFac`, `RatFacSpec`, `GoodAt`, `exists_good_primes`, `exists_good_prime`: for any finite set
   of integer matrices, every prime `q > q₀` avoids all denominators of the `E`'s and all
   numerators of their diagonals; `#ones Π = rank_ℚ A`.
2. `goodSub N` (rationals with denominator coprime to `N`), the ring hom `redHom N` to `ZMod N`,
   the total map `redQ N`, `redQ_matrix_identity`, `redQ_lower`, `isUnit_redQ`.
3. `FacAtZ` (the identity only mod `N`), `facAtZ_of_facAt`, the integer lifts `facZ Q`
   (entries `(redQ Q r).val`), the bridge `facAtZ_facZ`, and the re-proved chain
   `implΦ_eqZ`, `levelR_correct_amapZ`, `levelR_correctZ`, `prog_correctZ` (bounded level),
   `levelCost_eqZ`, `prog_costZ`, `prop11Z`, and the assembled `prop11_rat`.
-/

